# 📚 Books Market Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview
Books Market Analysis is an end-to-end data analytics project focused on collecting, cleaning, and analyzing book market data using Python.

The project uses web scraping and Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to understand book information and discover useful insights through visualizations.

## 🎯 Project Objectives
- Collect book data using web scraping.
- Clean and preprocess the scraped dataset.
- Perform Exploratory Data Analysis.
- Create visualizations to understand the data.
- Generate meaningful insights from the analysis.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- Python
- Requests
- BeautifulSoup
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Jupyter Notebook

## 📂 Project Structure
- `Books_Market_Analysis.ipynb` – Complete project notebook.
- `books_scraped.csv` – Raw scraped dataset.
- `books_cleaned.csv` – Cleaned dataset.
- `Visualizations/` – Generated charts and graphs.

## 📊 Visualizations
All generated charts and graphs are available in the Visualizations folder.

## 📈 Key Outcomes
- Collected book market data.
- Performed data cleaning and preprocessing.
- Analyzed the available book dataset.
- Created visualizations to present findings.

